Data   : MyActivityPageViewModel binds the shared S8 UserStore.myRecentActivity(params) (web useMyRecentActivity) via
         myActivityPageSourceOf(); the activity feed drives the page phase through asUiState. The committed date range
         (MyActivityPageViewModel.range, seeded from the web 30-day default `today-29 … today`) is the page's one piece of
         interaction state; combine(range, refreshTrigger) ▸ flatMapLatest ▸ source.myRecentActivity(activityParamsFor(range))
         re-reads on a range change (a new params cache key — web query re-keying) or on retry (web refetch). No HTTP in the view.
Adapt  : the web page's two configuration failures are reproduced 1:1 off the read's HTTP status, which the Android
         Resource→UiState mapping already carries as UiState.httpStatus: 503 ⇒ "Activity feed disabled" (web apiError.status===503),
         401 ⇒ "Identity required" (web apiError.status===401), any other failure ⇒ the error+Retry state. The error body uses the
         localized error.serverError.message in place of the web's raw apiError.message (an un-localizable technical string) —
         the only documented copy adaptation (Honesty Covenant #9); title/icon/retry remain web-faithful.
Feed   : the audit list delegates to the shared RecentActivityFeed surface (its own A3 parity unit), whose loading skeleton /
         empty / content states ARE the page's three declared data states. The shared-core UserActivityEntry rows are projected to
         the feed's render shape (MyActivityPage.toFeedEntry), dropping the ip / user_agent PII columns the feed never renders.
Range  : the web `actions={<RangePicker align="end" />}` is reproduced with the shared A3 RangePicker surface in the header row
         (DriveScorePage precedent) — beyond the 12 required parity items, included so the page is not scope-narrowed.
Nav    : feed-row click-through (web <Link to={entityHref(...)}>) routes through the ambient LocalDeepLinkRouter — the sanctioned
         page-host navigation seam (no LocalNavController is exposed to hosts; InboxPage / AlertRulesPage precedent): a tapped
         route like /vehicles/3 becomes a teslasync://app/vehicles/3 deep link the navigation shell consumes.
Strings: all 8 page keys already present in res/values/strings.xml (generated by apps/shared/i18n) — no string-catalog edit
         needed; every literal resolves via stringResource(R.string.translation_activity_myActivity_* / translation_common_retry).
Route  : Destinations 'myActivity' -> /me/activity pre-existing (Destinations.kt:172, NavGroup.System; count unchanged);
         host wired via PageHosts.register in TeslaSyncApplication.onCreate (idempotent), mirroring the sibling system hosts.

